¶
'''beard''' (bērd), ''v.'' [< late ME. ''berde;'' from the noun.] '''I.''' ''trans.'' '''1.''' To take by the beard; seize, pluck, or pull the beard of, in contempt or anger. Hence—'''2.''' Figuratively, to oppose to the face; set at defiance.

{{smaller block|It is to them most disgracefull, to be ''bearded'' of such a base varlett. {{right|''Spenser'', State of Ireland.}}
<poem>Dar’st thou then
To ''beard'' the lion in his den,</poem>}}

