'''3.''' To furnish with a beard, in any sense of the word.—'''4.''' In ''carp.'', to chip, plane, or otherwise diminish from a given line or to a given curve: as, to ''beard'' clamps, plank-sheers, etc.; in ''ship-building'', to round, as the adjacent parts of the rudder and stern-post, or the dead-wood, so as

